(A value parameter carries a type alongside its contents, so one function
 can take a number, a text or a decimal and ask which it was given. A
 value returned from a function carries its type back out, so it survives
 the trip in both directions.)

To describe with a value called item.
    If item is a number, print "number".
    Otherwise if item is a text, print "text".
    Otherwise print "decimal".

To echo with a value called item. Return a value, item.

A list called samples is [42, "hello", 3.14].

Print "Classifying each element:".
For each item in samples,
    describe of item.

A list called echoed is [].
For each item in samples,
    append echo of item to echoed.

Print "After round-trip through echo, still:".
For each item in echoed,
    describe of item.
